  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Deliver Brexit outside the single market/customs union with a Great Repeal Bill and ‘no deal better than a bad deal’; reduce net migration to the tens of thousands and tighten visas; balanced budget and low taxes; NHS +£8bn and major mental health commitments; energy price cap and 1.5m homes by 2022; defence ≥2% GDP and retain Trident. TEXT_D: Second referendum with option to remain; seek to stay in the single market/customs union; 1p income tax rise for NHS/social care; stronger pro-immigration stance (remove students from targets, post‑study visas); 300k homes/year; ambitious green agenda.",
